  "question": {
    "text": "An alkali is titrated against an acid with methyl orange as indicator, which of the following is a correct combination?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<table border=\"1\"><tr><td> Base</td><td> Acid</td><td> End point</td></tr><tr><td> Strong</td><td> Strong</td><td> Pink to colourless</td></tr></table>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<table border=\"1\"><tr><td> Base</td><td> Acid</td><td> End point</td></tr><tr><td> Weak</td><td> Strong</td><td> Colourless to pink</td></tr></table>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<table border=\"1\"><tr><td> Base</td><td> Acid</td><td> End point</td></tr><tr><td> Strong</td><td> Strong</td><td> Pinkish red to yellow</td></tr></table>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<table border=\"1\"><tr><td> Base</td><td> Acid</td><td> End point</td></tr><tr><td> Weak</td><td> Strong</td><td> Yellow to pinkish red</td></tr></table>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Methyl orange is weak organic base.  It is used in the titration of weak base vs strong acid.<br/><br/> <math><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mtext>Unionized form </mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtext>Yellow</mtext><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder></mrow></munder><mo>⇌</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mtext>Ionized form</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtext>Red</mtext><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder></mrow></munder></math> <br/><br/>In basic medium, equilibrium lies in backward direction and therefore it shows yellow colour.<br/><br/>In acidic medium, equilibrium shifts in forward direction and therefore, colour changes from yellow to red."
